(version 1)

# PicoEMP Rev-2026 custom design rules
#
# Upstream annotates SCH-PICOEMP-REV04.PDF with:
#     ISOLATION BARRIER, 400V MIN.  >1MM CLEARANCE PER 61010-1.
#
# That rule governs the ISOLATION BARRIER — HV side to logic side. It does not
# govern spacing *within* the HV section between two HV nets, which is bounded
# by component packages: an 0603 resistor has ~0.70 mm between its own pads, an
# 0805 ~0.80 mm, and the ATB3225 transformer 0.77 mm primary-to-secondary.
#
# Encoding the 1 mm figure as a plain netclass clearance is therefore wrong: it
# applies between any two differing nets touching the class, making 0603/0805
# parts illegal on HV nets. This rule scopes it correctly.
#
# Voltages, from primary sources (component ratings are headroom, not operating
# points — C3 is 630 V rated, Q2 650 V):
#   HV capacitor charge      ~250 V   (firmware/micropython/cspico_simple.py)
#   Barrier design rating     400 V   (upstream schematic annotation)
#   Hi-pot proof test           1 kV  ("well beyond the voltages the device can
#                                      generate" — hardware/design_notes)

(rule "HV isolation barrier"
	(constraint clearance (min 1.0mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'HV' && B.NetClass != 'HV'"))

# The barrier also applies to the board edge, where a HV net could otherwise
# creep to an exposed cut edge.
(rule "HV to board edge"
	(constraint edge_clearance (min 1.0mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'HV'"))
